\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces For \textbf  {RQ3}, this experiment tests whether changing demographic descriptors in 65 otherwise matched adverse-outcome scenarios changes their causal CAA projections. Values are mean paired differences from the White-male condition $\pm $ the bootstrap 95\% CI half-width; positive values indicate greater alignment with the causal direction, and bold entries have CIs that exclude zero. \textbf  {Main takeaway: projections differ reliably for several contrasts, but these associations alone do not demonstrate biased behavior or a causal mechanism.}}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rq3}{{1}{4}{For \textbf {RQ3}, this experiment tests whether changing demographic descriptors in 65 otherwise matched adverse-outcome scenarios changes their causal CAA projections. Values are mean paired differences from the White-male condition $\pm $ the bootstrap 95\% CI half-width; positive values indicate greater alignment with the causal direction, and bold entries have CIs that exclude zero. \textbf {Main takeaway: projections differ reliably for several contrasts, but these associations alone do not demonstrate biased behavior or a causal mechanism.}}{table.1}{}}
